\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Gentle Jesus, meek and mild,
\par Look upon a little child,
\par Pity my simplicity,
\par Suffer me to come to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Fain I would to Thee be brought;
\par Gracious Lord, forbid it not;
\par In the kingdom of Thy grace
\par Give a little child a place.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Fain I would be as Thou art;
\par Give me Thy obedient heart:
\par Thou art pitiful and kind;
\par Let me have Thy loving mind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Let me above all fufil
\par God my heavenly Father's will;
\par Never His good Spirit grieve,
\par Only to His glory live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lamb of God, I look to Thee;
\par Thou shalt my example be:
\par Thou art gentle, meek, and mild;
\par Thou was once a little child.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thou didst live to God alone;
\par Thou didst never seek Thine own;
\par Thou Thyself didst never please:
\par God was all Thy happiness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Loving Jesus, gentle Lamb,
\par In Thy gracious hands I am:
\par Make me, Saviour, what Thou art;
\par Live Thyself within my heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. I shall then show forth Thy praise,
\par Serve Thee all my happy days;
\par Then the world shall always see
\par Christ, the holy Child, in me.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

